for row in rows:t+='| '+' | '.join(x.replace('|','\\|') for x in row)+' |\n'
t+='\n## Input recipes and evidence\n\n'
t+='**H1.** The item manifest is `items/devs1_routed.json`; it embeds the questions, answers and membership. Its sources are `items_sources/CAMERA_TASKS.jsonl`, `items_sources/TASKS.jsonl` and `items_sources/c8r_inventory.json`. The supplied descendant package records those relative names at '+c('items/devs1_routed.json',54179,A)+', '+c('items/devs1_routed.json',54183,A)+'; its loader pins them at '+c('h1eval/items.py',11,A)+' and builds the 636-item manifest at '+c('h1eval/items.py',132,A)+'.\n\n'
t+='The old H1-0 payload is explicitly located at `O/e6fc152498/p446`, with a partial Trinity copy at `trinity-1-3:/scratch/jjyeung/orch_n30/notseen_diag/work/f3/p446` ('+c('H1_0_NOT_SEEN_DIAGNOSIS_20261117.md',3)+'). The source kit item directory is `trinity-3-30:/scratch/jjyeung/orch_n30/h1_headsft/kit/items/` ('+c('H1_GT_HEAD_ROUTING_SFT_20261116.md',3)+'; '+c('H1_GT_HEAD_ROUTING_SFT_20261116.md',86)+'). The bf94 re-pin records `a/export.json` ('+c('H1_GT_HEAD_ROUTING_SFT_20261116.md',104)+'); its exact Orchard payload directory is not recorded. Do not substitute H1-0 export pins for H1-1.\n\n'
t+='A locally supplied candidate manifest is `'+str(A/'items/devs1_routed.json')+'`. Its 1,440,816 bytes and SHA256 `2849206e3eb66f40b3e2fba49cfe84abe3c0465a318f85aaeaeca6ff6f26fe21` are measured locally and agree with published INDEX line 7. The published provenance also records CAMERA_TASKS as 801,941 bytes / `f59090ffc8fd0f4d80a2b049e2624660c0f46dbc1d26016145f4747850a432ac`, and TASKS as 1,992,844 bytes / `a2f3fdbdab06ab81942d44044d85090df8ec5b86908cf010cdbcb17e35637f5e`. These are candidate shared task inputs, not proof of an old return join. Every return item_mapping task_sha256 must match before reuse.\n\n'
t+='Keep each return’s SUMMARY/COMPLETE, IDENTITY, EXPORT_PIN/RETURN_ID if present, journal item_mapping and environment files. The kit report is the package scorer’s curve/report, not another input population. For 170706 the records name `O/e6fc152498/r2/sj/h10sub3_b01ec87a6f29b00029ad2/` and Trinity `h10_score/work/results/170706/`; for 170846 they name `curve.json` (3e07ff05) and `cont_ops/work/m2pair/out/B_minus_A_170846.md`. The precise Orchard report path for 170846 is unrecorded. '+c('H1_GT_HEAD_ROUTING_SFT_20261116.md',103)+'; '+c('H1_GT_HEAD_ROUTING_SFT_20261116.md',104)+'.\n\n'
t+='**VSTI.** Required population: `agent/vstibench_repr_450_v3.json`, SHA prefix d7c16986, 450 items / nine types. The record gives a repo-relative item filename, not its Orchard absolute path. The kit’s bound task file path must be obtained from the returned request/metadata; it is not safe to invent a `j0/tasks.jsonl`. Kit report: `trinity-1-3:/scratch/jjyeung/orch_n30/native_r4/work/ret4/report_v1d/report/REPORT.md`; scorer proof `builds/01_vsti/out/SCORER_CHECK.json` in that lane. '+c('VSTI_NATIVE_CAMERA_READ_STEP544_20261116.md',3)+'; '+c('VSTI_NATIVE_CAMERA_READ_STEP544_20261116.md',9)+'; '+c('VSTI_NATIVE_CAMERA_READ_STEP544_20261116.md',12)+'; '+c('VSTI_NATIVE_CAMERA_READ_STEP544_20261116.md',15)+'. Raw j0 rows survive; the current selector ignores j0 entirely.\n\n'
t+='**PROBE.** `native/probe/items.jsonl` and root COMPLETE are known; job, item manifest, task file, request filename and report filename are not. Read the return’s small JSON metadata using command R below, then fetch only the exact bound input paths it actually names. The step-544 label alone cannot identify a population. '+c('IDENT.txt',62,I)+'.\n\n'
t+='**PILOT.** Inspect the pilot SPEC, COMPLETE, task/membership documents and `report/*.json`; keep `report/B2048.json` for category and score checks. Offread takes question/truth from each result row, so external tasks are required only if those fields are absent, plus the exact pilot manifest for completeness. IDENT does not name a separate Orchard input package. The production siblings’ task inputs cannot establish pilot membership. pb906 is the exact proof token in the ReVSI record; pb59 is not explicitly matched to job 169991. Production lane roots are `trinity-1-3:/scratch/jjyeung/orch_n30/evalx27/work/kit/build/a8acc277397/` and `.../kit_revsi/build/a348bc58686/`; the common kit record names build R’s `package_vsi.tar` and `package_revsi.tar`, not the pilot’s absolute package path. '+c('OFFICIAL_VSI_DIRECT_STEP544_20261115.md',27)+'; '+c('REVSI_DIRECT_STEP544_20261115.md',24)+'; '+c('OFFICIAL_READ_KIT_B07_20261116.md',11)+'.\n\n'
t+='**HEAD.** K1 needs capture/manifest evidence rather than question manifests. The recorded inputs/outputs are `/scratch/jjyeung/k1/run_tower_sam_2`, `/scratch/jjyeung/k1/own_170235/native/probe`, `/scratch/jjyeung/k1/run_convert_2` on trinity-1-18, with the verified trinity-3-30 mirror `/scratch/jjyeung/n30_mirror/k1_ops3/`; analysis reports are `work/kc_guard/guard_downstream/analyses/{primary_296,sensitivity_300}/REPORT.json`. No input fetch can turn prefill-only output into model generation traces. '+c('K1_KILL_TEST_RUN_20261116.md',55)+'; '+c('K1_KILL_TEST_RUN_20261116.md',58)+'; '+c('K1_KILL_TEST_RUN_20261116.md',63)+'; '+c('K1_KILL_TEST_RUN_20261116.md',69)+'.\n\n'
t+='**EMPTY / INDEXED.** Empty returns require no task fetch for corpus generation; retain their failure receipts. Indexed reads require no duplicate fetch. All IDENT entries, including published siblings, are accounted for in the table.\n\n'
t+='## Adapter limitations verified against the supplied source\n\n'
t+='The flat routed journal names in IDENT do not match `ROUTE_ROW` at '+c('ingest_read.py',163,I)+'. A routed extension must map the single-read layout, identity, mapping and completion paths consistently; merely supplying --inputs cannot fix detection. The native adapter detects only `native/paired/results/items.jsonl` ('+c('ingest_read.py',615,I)+') and consumes only that path plus native/R1.json ('+c('ingest_read.py',630,I)+'). Both j0 and native/probe need explicit adapters or an audited path normalization. Preserve original source names and validate actual required arms; do not synthesize paired arms.\n\n'
t+='The offread adapter reads a0 and three budget paths, while pb59 also contains b0/d0 journals. The actual b0/d0 `items_b0.jsonl` names also fail KitAdapter’s `items_a0.jsonl` regex, so extend source selection and arm handling deliberately. Offread sets official=true by default ('+c('ingest_read.py',583,I)+'); pilot metadata must explicitly override it to false. The source cannot infer that proof jobs are official benchmark reads.\n\n'
t+='## Exact read-only commands for the Orchard owner\n\n'
t+='Run these in an already-authorized Orchard session. They write no Orchard files and submit no jobs. The output carries only small inputs/metadata; capture stdout with the owner’s existing transport. Commands use recorded roots and inspect names before requesting absent files. No transfer or remote presence check was performed in this audit.\n\n'
t+='**P: discover and fetch H1 package metadata.** The root is recorded in the diagnosis. Relative package directories are evidenced in the supplied loader/manifest, but their presence inside p446 is unverified. This bounded command reports missing directories, emits the actual filenames, sizes, hashes and base64 bytes, and does not follow symlinks or read model/frame payloads. This avoids asserting an unrecorded full file path.\n\n```bash\ndate -u\nnice -n 10 env CUDA_VISIBLE_DEVICES="" OMP_NUM_THREADS=8 MKL_NUM_THREADS=8 OPENBLAS_NUM_THREADS=8 TOKENIZERS_PARALLELISM=false PYTHONDONTWRITEBYTECODE=1 python3 -I -s -B - <<\'PY\'\n'
t+='from pathlib import Path\nimport base64, hashlib, json, sys\nroot = Path("/project/community/jjyeung/okh7/e6fc152498/p446")\ntotal = 0\nfor rel in (".", "items", "items_sources", "a"):\n    folder = root / rel\n    if not folder.is_dir():\n        print("UNRESOLVED_DIRECTORY " + str(folder), file=sys.stderr)\n        continue\n    for p in sorted(folder.iterdir()):\n        if p.is_symlink() or not p.is_file() or p.suffix not in (".json", ".jsonl"):\n            continue\n        size = p.stat().st_size\n        if size > 8*1024*1024 or total+size > 16*1024*1024:\n            print("SIZE_LIMIT " + str(p), file=sys.stderr)\n            continue\n        b=p.read_bytes(); total += len(b)\n        print(json.dumps({"path":str(p), "bytes":len(b), "sha256":hashlib.sha256(b).hexdigest(), "base64":base64.b64encode(b).decode()}))\nPY\n```\n\n'
t+='**R: fetch small binding/manifest/report members from the recorded return archives.** Use the helper below once per chosen archive, serially. It lists all member names and sizes to stderr and sends selected small metadata bytes to stdout. It reads the compressed return on Orchard, but sends no generation rows, geometry, frames or weights. Supply exactly one recorded path from the table. For example:\n\n```bash\ndate -u\nnice -n 10 env CUDA_VISIBLE_DEVICES="" OMP_NUM_THREADS=8 MKL_NUM_THREADS=8 OPENBLAS_NUM_THREADS=8 TOKENIZERS_PARALLELISM=false PYTHONDONTWRITEBYTECODE=1 python3 -I -s -B - /project/community/jjyeung/okh7/n2r/d627d31523064791d2ce3456/result.tar.gz <<\'PY\'\n'
t+='import base64, hashlib, json, re, sys, tarfile\ntotal=0\nwith tarfile.open(sys.argv[1], "r|*") as archive:\n    for m in archive:\n        print(json.dumps({"member":m.name,"bytes":m.size,"regular":m.isfile()}), file=sys.stderr)\n        name=m.name.lstrip("./")\n        base=name.rsplit("/",1)[-1]\n        selected=(base in {"SPEC.json","SUMMARY.json","COMPLETE.json","FAILED.json","IDENTITY.json","EXPORT_PIN.json","RETURN_ID.json","READ_IDENTITY.json","ORCHARD_NATIVE.json","ORCHARD_LAUNCHER.json","CARDS.json","READ_PLAN.json","environment.json","request.json","item_mapping.json","curve.json"} or re.search(r"(^|/)(items|items_sources|report)/[^/]+\\.(json|jsonl)$", name) or base in {"TASKS.jsonl","CAMERA_TASKS.jsonl"})\n        if not m.isfile() or not selected or m.size>8*1024*1024 or total+m.size>16*1024*1024:\n            continue\n        b=archive.extractfile(m).read(); total+=len(b)\n        print(json.dumps({"archive":sys.argv[1],"member":m.name,"bytes":len(b),"sha256":hashlib.sha256(b).hexdigest(),"base64":base64.b64encode(b).decode()}))\nPY\n```\n\n'
